{
  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With zero completed experiments, the priority is to establish a strong anchor configuration that maximizes the number of clean one-at-a-time comparisons available for subsequent experiments. config_001 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) uses the simplest and most standard choices across all variable sub-dimensions: PCA as the baseline RNA encoder, ViT-L as a strong standard image encoder, avgpool as the simplest aggregation, and concat as the simplest fusion. This makes it a natural reference point: config_002 isolates the image encoder (resnet50 vs ViT-L), config_020 isolates fusion (weighted vs concat), config_041 isolates aggregation (transformer vs avgpool), config_050 isolates RNA encoder (scgpt vs PCA), and config_034 isolates RNA encoder (scvi_n200 vs PCA). Starting with this 'simplest full pipeline' also avoids conflating the effect of multimodal fusion with the effect of complex sub-choices, so that if performance is weak, a follow-up unimodal baseline (e.g., config_009 or config_018) can cleanly attribute the gap to fusion vs. individual modality quality. Under a limited budget, this single experiment reduces the most uncertainty about the overall pipeline while preserving the greatest number of informative next steps."
}

